ABSD per-port patch for sbase 0.1 ed (userland/README.md, "Patches").

Failure: (1) ed installs SIGINT/SIGHUP/SIGQUIT handlers with sigaction,
which neither the kit nor the adapter defines (userland/DEMAND.tsv: ed
sigaction REFUSED, link-time). (2) The scratch file that holds the buffer
is mkstemp("$TMPDIR/ed.XXXXXX"), defaulting to /tmp; on ABSD the
environment is empty and /tmp is a read-only ancestor (C-INTERFACE.md 6,
CPA-045), so ed could not hold any text, and the failure only printed "?"
and left ed running without a buffer. (3) !cmd and w !cmd call system()
and popen(), which the adapter refuses at run time (CPA-003): ed would
print "?" with "bad exec", or nothing at all for !cmd.

Change: (1) with ABSD_NO_SIGNALS (the ABSD build) no handler is installed.
No signal is ever delivered on ABSD (CPA-004): ^C in an SSH session ends
the pipeline and ed with it, so the buffer is lost unless written, and
the scratch file stays behind in its directory. (2) the scratch file is
created in $TMPDIR when that is set and non-empty, else in the working
directory ("./ed.XXXXXX"), never in /tmp (owner D2: per-port patch, no
contract change); if it cannot be created when ed starts, ed exits with
status 1 and "ed: cannot create scratch file ./ed.XXXXXX (start ed in a
writable directory): <strerror>". (3) !cmd and w !cmd are refused before
anything runs: "?" and, with h or H, "shell commands are not supported on
this system" (no spawn right). (2) and (3) apply to both builds, so the
host reference pins exactly what ABSD must do.

Preserved: every editing command, the buffer and undo behaviour, file
reads and writes, the "?" error convention and the exit status (1 after
any error). The scratch file is still removed on q, Q and end of input.
On Linux the reference behaves as upstream except that, with TMPDIR
unset, the scratch file lives in the working directory, and that ! is
refused. No adapter or kit change. dowrite's `sh ? pclose(fp) : fclose(fp)`
arms stay; `sh` is never set now, so the optimised build drops pclose (an -O0
build would still name it; the adapter defines it, -1/ECHILD).

--- a/ed.c
+++ b/ed.c
@@ -376,17 +376,28 @@
 {
 	int r, k;
 	char *dir;
+	static int started;
 
 	clearbuf();
 	clearundo();
-	if ((dir = getenv("TMPDIR")) == NULL)
-		dir = "/tmp";
+	/* ABSD (userland/patches/ed-absd.patch): the scratch file goes in
+	   TMPDIR when it is set, else in the working directory, never in
+	   /tmp (owner D2; C-INTERFACE.md 6: /tmp is not writable, the
+	   environment is empty). Failing to create it when ed starts is
+	   fatal and named: an ed without its scratch file cannot hold text. */
+	if ((dir = getenv("TMPDIR")) == NULL || *dir == '\0')
+		dir = ".";
 	r = snprintf(tmpname, sizeof(tmpname), "%s/%s",
 	             dir, "ed.XXXXXX");
 	if (r < 0 || (size_t)r >= sizeof(tmpname))
 		error("scratch filename too long");
-	if ((scratch = mkstemp(tmpname)) < 0)
+	if ((scratch = mkstemp(tmpname)) < 0) {
+		if (!started)
+			eprintf("cannot create scratch file %s "
+			        "(start ed in a writable directory):", tmpname);
 		error("failed to create scratch file");
+	}
+	started = 1;
 	if ((k = makeline(NULL, NULL)))
 		error("input/output error in scratch file");
 	relink(k, k, k, k);
@@ -761,10 +772,9 @@
 	}
 
 	if(fname[0] == '!') {
-		sh = 1;
-		fname++;
-		if((fp = popen(fname, "w")) == NULL)
-			error("bad exec");
+		/* ABSD (userland/patches/ed-absd.patch): w !cmd is refused
+		   like !cmd: no spawn right (CPA-003). Both builds. */
+		error("shell commands are not supported on this system");
 	} else {
 		sh = 0;
 		if ((fp = fopen(fname, "w")) == NULL)
@@ -1091,11 +1101,11 @@
 	}
 	addchar('\0', &cmd);
 
-	if (repl)
-		puts(cmd.str);
-	system(cmd.str);
-	if (optdiag)
-		puts("!");
+	/* ABSD (userland/patches/ed-absd.patch): a program holds no spawn
+	   right, so !cmd is refused before anything runs (CPA-003). Both
+	   builds, so the reference pins the refusal. */
+	(void)repl;
+	error("shell commands are not supported on this system");
 }
 
